 Summary of changes:
   - Fixed `saveVariantPrompt`: In the listing creation page, the action to save the updated subtype
     detection prompt now uses dispatchBroadcast instead of a local store dispatch. This ensures the change
     is persisted to Firestore and synchronized across all users.
   - Improved `dispatchBroadcast`: Updated the dispatchBroadcast implementation in the listing detail page
     to support thunks. This ensures that any thunk dispatched through it (like those for title or
     description regeneration) correctly broadcasts its internal actions.
   - Synchronized Review Start: The handleStartReview action in the listing creation page now uses
     dispatchBroadcast to ensure that starting a review batch is reflected for all connected users.
   - Verified Prompt Persistence: Confirmed that title and description prompt updates are correctly
     broadcasted whenever a regeneration is triggered, as the underlying thunks use the provided
     broadcast-capable dispatch.
